<gpx version="1.1" creator="galicica.finereli.com" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:gpxx="http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/GpxExtensions/v3" xmlns:gpx_style="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/gpx_style/0/2">
<metadata><name>Velestovo - Krstec - Tri Mazhi peak - Studino - Elshani</name><desc>A long combined tour through nearly every kind of habitat in the park. The start and the end face west; higher up you walk along ridges, through dense belts of forest and across wide open karst fields. You gain most of the height at the start, and after that the ups and downs are gentle enough for relaxed walking. The ground is hard and stony, grassy in places. On the ridge path from Krstec to Cresha it's firm earth and stones, and the middle section is mostly rocky. Excellent views over all of Galičica and the wider region. https://galicica.finereli.com/routes/velestovo-krstec-tri-mazhi-studino-elshani/</desc><link href="https://galicica.finereli.com/"><text>galicica.finereli.com</text></link><copyright author="NP Galičica (trail lines), OpenStreetMap contributors (places, G-6)"><license>https://galicica.finereli.com/about/#license</license></copyright></metadata>
<wpt lat="41.083602" lon="20.828031"><name>Start: Velestovo village</name><desc>Velestovo village to Elshani village: 16.8 km, 7 h, moderate</desc><sym>Trail Head</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="41.026276" lon="20.816523"><name>Start: Elshani village</name><desc>Elshani village to Velestovo village: 16.8 km, 7 h 30 min, moderate</desc><sym>Trail Head</sym></wpt>
<trk><name>G-2: the T-3 junction to the Chereshnana junction</name><desc>G-2 is one of Galičica National Park's high ridge trails above 1,600 m. It's 3.9 km from the T-3 junction to the Chereshnana junction, with about 135 m of climbing and 226 m of descent in the direction drawn, between 1,395 m and 1,617 m.</desc><type>G</type><extensions><gpxx:TrackExtension><gpxx:DisplayColor>Yellow</gpxx:DisplayColor></gpxx:TrackExtension><gpx_style:line><gpx_style:color>D4A20B</gpx_style:color><gpx_style:width>4</gpx_style:width></gpx_style:line></extensions><trkseg><trkpt lat="41.076230" lon="20.846640"><ele>1488</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.076157" lon="20.846653"><ele>1488</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.076081" lon="20.846706"><ele>1491</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.076010" lon="20.846689"><ele>1494</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.076020" lon="20.846619"><ele>1493</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.076003" lon="20.846608"><ele>1493</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075918" lon="20.846661"><ele>1498</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075798" lon="20.846642"><ele>1502</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075753" lon="20.846626"><ele>1503</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075727" lon="20.846575"><ele>1503</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075635" lon="20.846581"><ele>1506</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075550" lon="20.846593"><ele>1509</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075498" lon="20.846567"><ele>1510</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075434" lon="20.846622"><ele>1512</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075433" lon="20.846624"><ele>1512</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075416" lon="20.846658"><ele>1512</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075295" lon="20.846556"><ele>1515</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075262" lon="20.846556"><ele>1516</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075234" lon="20.846448"><ele>1517</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075198" lon="20.846414"><ele>1518</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075190" lon="20.846401"><ele>1519</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075183" lon="20.846388"><ele>1519</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.075178" lon="20.846379"><ele>1519</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="